  B0 the log line begins: USER        PID ACCESS COMMAND ...
  B1 fuser -vm on the unmounted mount point: 19 lines kept of the record (of 1000 chars); mounts under the alternate root: []
     fuser's whole output: 92 lines; its first: 'USER        PID ACCESS COMMAND'; 'kernel mount /' in it: True
     the summary's 'held by': the line 'python3', cut at the 1000-character tail
  B2 'busy' in the output decides a retry:
     "cannot export 'skzreplay': pool is busy": retried
     "cannot unmount '/w/alt/skz': pool or dataset is busy": retried
     'umount: /w/alt/skz: target is busy.': retried
     "cannot export 'skzreplay': I/O error": straight to -f
     'internal error: Device or resource busy': retried
     'TIMEOUT after 120s': straight to -f
